1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,570
(All people, organizations, businesses,
events, and places shown are fictional.)

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,005
(Child actors filmed in a safe space
with their guardians present.)

3
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:08,675
Make it hot, please.

4
00:00:09,376 --> 00:00:10,544
Really hot.

5
00:00:11,512 --> 00:00:13,247
(We support actor Tak Mu I
and the "Rooftop Romance" team!)

6
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:25,492
(Go, Tak Mu I!)

7
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,857
Blisters are unavoidable.

8
00:00:57,157 --> 00:00:59,960
For three to four days,
you may have sharp pain,

9
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:03,330
burning, stinging,
and things of that nature.

10
00:01:03,797 --> 00:01:05,572
If it hurts too much,
don't tough it out.

11
00:01:05,596 --> 00:01:07,901
Take the painkillers
I'm prescribing.

12
00:01:08,468 --> 00:01:10,237
Doctor, will it leave a scar?

13
00:01:10,671 --> 00:01:12,246
She shouldn't scar,

14
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:14,374
but her legs may end up
with slight discoloration.

15
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:19,580
You seem very shaken, so I'll give you
a sedative shot before you're discharged.

16
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:22,382
- Thank you.
- Sure.

17
00:01:28,689 --> 00:01:31,558
You had to go through such an ordeal
on set because of me…

18
00:01:32,192 --> 00:01:33,427
I'm really okay.

19
00:01:33,827 --> 00:01:35,262
She said it won't even scar.

20
00:01:36,463 --> 00:01:40,267
By the way, who was that woman, anyway?

21
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:43,704
She's playing a minor role
with a line or two,

22
00:01:44,037 --> 00:01:47,508
but I thought it was odd when she came
to set, even though we didn't need her.

23
00:01:47,841 --> 00:01:51,011
Now I'm realizing that she was…
there just to see Mr. Tak.

24
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,512
I'm sorry.

25
00:01:55,382 --> 00:01:58,852
But why on earth did she do that to me?

26
00:01:59,686 --> 00:02:01,688
I don't get it either, honestly.

27
00:02:03,257 --> 00:02:06,193
I told you, I'll tell you everything
once you bring Tak Mu I.

28
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:09,897
What do you mean, everything?

29
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:12,733
I'm asking why you splashed the coffee,
young lady!

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,068
Don't call me "young lady."
It's Song Yun O.

31
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:19,706
Fine, yes.

32
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:22,442
Ms. Song, why did you do that?

33
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:25,012
Please call my man Mu I.

34
00:02:25,212 --> 00:02:27,147
"My man?"
Excuse me.

35
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:29,783
You're here on assault charges right now!

36
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:32,819
Who are you to tell a man like him
to come all the way here?

37
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,689
He won't come! He won't!

38
00:02:35,756 --> 00:02:36,723
(Police)

39
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:40,360
- As I said…
- Sir, look, it's Tak…

40
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,828
- What?
- It's Tak Mu I, Tak…

41
00:02:58,846 --> 00:02:59,880
Why did you do it?

42
00:03:01,114 --> 00:03:03,550
"You're pretty. You could be a celebrity."

43
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,886
I grew up hearing that all the time.

44
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:10,891
So I believed I was a flower… all along.

45
00:03:12,626 --> 00:03:15,629
A flower… meant to fully bloom one day.

46
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:20,667
Hello, I'm the new actor Song Yun O.

47
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:22,130
I look forward to working with you.

48
00:03:25,606 --> 00:03:27,908
Hello, I'm the new actor Song Yun O.

49
00:03:27,908 --> 00:03:29,209
I look forward to…

50
00:03:30,611 --> 00:03:32,679
Hello.

51
00:03:33,981 --> 00:03:36,316
But when I got to the set,

52
00:03:37,851 --> 00:03:40,020
I realized I wasn't a flower,
but only grass.

53
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,656
Nameless grass.

54
00:03:47,794 --> 00:03:48,795
Goodness. I'm sorry.

55
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:51,732
You should apologize to this lady.

56
00:03:52,633 --> 00:03:54,268
Yes, of course. Sorry about that.

57
00:03:58,705 --> 00:04:01,308
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

58
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:05,746
I love the color of your shoes.

59
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:16,089
How could you forget me
after all that?

60
00:04:16,356 --> 00:04:19,092
And why haven't you eaten the food
I've been sending you?

61
00:04:19,626 --> 00:04:22,362
You said actors are hungry all day
because that's the job…

62
00:04:24,865 --> 00:04:26,533
The wait is so long.

63
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:28,468
I'm so hungry.

64
00:04:29,236 --> 00:04:31,205
But for us actors, that's the job, right?

65
00:04:34,374 --> 00:04:36,436
You don't eat,

66
00:04:36,503 --> 00:04:39,068
and that's why you keep losing weight.

67
00:04:42,082 --> 00:04:43,050
Why is that?

68
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:45,219
Did that convenience store girl
tell you not to eat?

69
00:04:47,087 --> 00:04:49,156
Did you forget me because of her?

70
00:04:50,265 --> 00:04:51,269
(Chaeun Salad)

71
00:04:51,336 --> 00:04:52,459
Just this, please.

72
00:04:55,329 --> 00:04:58,131
- That'll be $6.
- Have a good day.

73
00:04:59,933 --> 00:05:03,570
Another supply truck is coming in
a little later, at around 4 PM.

74
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:06,473
If you come then, you can buy
a salad lunch box.

75
00:05:09,409 --> 00:05:10,410
Hello.

76
00:05:15,716 --> 00:05:18,685
Why were you only looking at her? Why?

77
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:23,390
How far must I go…

78
00:05:24,424 --> 00:05:26,827
for you to finally see
how I feel about you?

79
00:05:27,394 --> 00:05:28,629
Mu I.

80
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:31,765
I love you.

81
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,572
You're sure he's safe, right?

82
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:41,708
What could possibly go wrong?

83
00:05:42,743 --> 00:05:44,011
The handcuffs are on tight,

84
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,046
and we're watching from here.

85
00:05:47,981 --> 00:05:49,016
I just realized…

86
00:05:50,117 --> 00:05:51,084
I need to stop now.

87
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:57,824
I need to stop being kind.

88
00:06:02,462 --> 00:06:03,497
Now that I know…

89
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:07,534
my kindness can hurt other people,

90
00:06:09,436 --> 00:06:10,522
I have to stop.

91
00:06:17,911 --> 00:06:20,247
Detective, you're watching, right?

92
00:06:23,016 --> 00:06:24,785
There will be no leniency.

93
00:06:24,955 --> 00:06:26,799
I'd also like to request
a restraining order.

94
00:06:29,356 --> 00:06:30,390
What do you mean by that?

95
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,783
Mu I, I was wrong.

96
00:06:31,807 --> 00:06:32,893
I won't ever do it again.

97
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:34,728
Don't, please don't.

98
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:36,129
You don't mean it, right?

99
00:06:36,129 --> 00:06:37,931
- Let go.
- I was wrong, Mu I.

100
00:06:37,931 --> 00:06:38,966
- I'm sorry.
- Mu I.

101
00:06:38,966 --> 00:06:41,134
- Mu I, I was wrong.
- Out, get out!

102
00:06:41,134 --> 00:06:42,236
- Mu I!
- Let go!

103
00:06:42,236 --> 00:06:43,237
Let go!

104
00:06:43,604 --> 00:06:45,806
Hey, let go! Mu I!

105
00:06:55,616 --> 00:06:56,783
No, don't get up.

106
00:07:00,787 --> 00:07:01,922
Where's Producer Yeon Ju?

107
00:07:02,789 --> 00:07:05,058
She said she had to go to the editing bay…

108
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:10,931
How's the wound?

109
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:13,600
It's fine.

110
00:07:13,901 --> 00:07:15,660
She said it won't even scar,

111
00:07:15,684 --> 00:07:17,070
because you poured water
on it right away.

112
00:07:17,571 --> 00:07:18,982
I'm not as concerned about the scarring.

113
00:07:19,007 --> 00:07:20,208
You're in pain.

114
00:07:20,374 --> 00:07:21,408
I'm not in pain at all.

115
00:07:24,311 --> 00:07:28,749
I heard Yeon Ju on the phone
with your manager earlier.

116
00:07:29,516 --> 00:07:32,619
He told her reasons you couldn't help
mistaking me for a stalker.

117
00:07:34,922 --> 00:07:37,991
Also, I should've brought this up earlier.

118
00:07:38,892 --> 00:07:40,427
At Gohyang Diner,

119
00:07:41,195 --> 00:07:45,165
I knew you were the masked man
who helped me fend off the condom guy,

120
00:07:45,899 --> 00:07:47,634
but I was so shocked at the time.

121
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:51,171
And given the situation,
I couldn't say thank you.

122
00:07:53,841 --> 00:07:56,276
A lot has happened to us already.

123
00:07:57,544 --> 00:07:58,512
That's true.

124
00:08:00,614 --> 00:08:03,417
I'm sorry that you went
through this because of me.

125
00:08:04,117 --> 00:08:05,953
It must be so hard,

126
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:08,388
living as a celebrity.

127
00:08:15,562 --> 00:08:16,563
Here.

128
00:08:41,522 --> 00:08:45,859
I'll take this because it seems
doing so will put your mind at ease.

129
00:08:46,927 --> 00:08:47,895
Thank you.

130
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:01,308
This will sting.

131
00:09:05,445 --> 00:09:06,413
Thank you.

132
00:09:10,784 --> 00:09:12,519
Try these on.

133
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,321
Sure, okay.

134
00:09:20,761 --> 00:09:23,263
- Let me help you.
- What? No…

135
00:09:43,217 --> 00:09:44,251
Let me take you home.

136
00:09:45,052 --> 00:09:47,054
It's okay. I can get home on my own.

137
00:09:48,956 --> 00:09:50,824
See? I can walk just fine.

138
00:09:51,258 --> 00:09:53,227
One, two, one, two.

139
00:09:59,366 --> 00:10:02,369
So this is what it's like
to ride in a celebrity's car.

140
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:08,008
(Radio FM 12.1 Good Music for a Good Day)

141
00:10:08,008 --> 00:10:10,677
What? It's Ian Kim.
I'm a huge fan.

142
00:10:11,745 --> 00:10:14,648
Really? So am I.

143
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:17,251
He's the only singer I've ever liked
my whole life.

144
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:20,254
Why did you like Ian Kim?

145
00:10:21,855 --> 00:10:23,390
Well, first of all,

146
00:10:23,924 --> 00:10:26,426
he sings well
and also has a great speaking voice,

147
00:10:26,827 --> 00:10:29,463
and more than anything,
all of his song lyrics are so good.

148
00:10:29,930 --> 00:10:31,465
Lyrics that pierce your heart.

149
00:10:31,899 --> 00:10:33,087
Have you been to his concert?

150
00:10:33,111 --> 00:10:34,535
It's absolutely amazing.

151
00:10:36,503 --> 00:10:38,038
I almost went, but…

152
00:11:09,403 --> 00:11:13,240
(Ian Kim CONCERT)

153
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:27,521
What's on your mind?

154
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:31,976
I'm thinking, if I'd known
it was his final show,

155
00:11:32,043 --> 00:11:33,450
I would've gone.

156
00:11:33,861 --> 00:11:35,095
Or something like that.

157
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,531
He did retire so suddenly.

158
00:11:38,765 --> 00:11:41,468
We just heard Ian Kim's
"Let's Walk Slowly."

159
00:11:41,535 --> 00:11:43,136
His return after 7 years is all the buzz.

160
00:11:43,637 --> 00:11:46,540
Concert tickets reportedly sold out
within the first 10 minutes,

161
00:11:46,807 --> 00:11:48,508
so he seems to be as popular as ever.

162
00:11:48,575 --> 00:11:50,744
- He's making a comeback?
- Here's another Ian Kim song.

163
00:11:50,811 --> 00:11:51,812
Sold out again.

164
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:53,814
I won't be able to go again.

165
00:11:57,718 --> 00:12:00,254
Hey, may I look at these books?

166
00:12:00,654 --> 00:12:02,389
Books? Yes, sure.

167
00:12:03,857 --> 00:12:05,459
("Star and the Half Moon 1")

168
00:12:09,596 --> 00:12:13,734
They tear even when I turn them gently,
so I tape them back again and again.

169
00:12:14,468 --> 00:12:15,469
It's a mess, isn't it?

170
00:12:21,742 --> 00:12:23,377
About the third book.

171
00:12:25,279 --> 00:12:29,816
I worked part-time during college
in a building with many publisher offices.

172
00:12:30,417 --> 00:12:33,487
I saw the book discarded
at the recycling area, so I took it home.

173
00:12:34,021 --> 00:12:35,756
Okay, I see.

174
00:12:37,255 --> 00:12:38,384
Listen,

175
00:12:38,451 --> 00:12:40,594
I don't know if I should ask you this now,

176
00:12:41,028 --> 00:12:42,896
but could you lend it to me
just this once?

177
00:12:43,397 --> 00:12:45,465
I'll keep it clean and give it back.

178
00:12:46,033 --> 00:12:48,135
Two days. No, one day is enough.

179
00:12:48,535 --> 00:12:49,670
No.

180
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:53,640
There must be a reason the author
didn't put it out into the world.

181
00:12:53,841 --> 00:12:54,808
Maybe it's embarrassing.

182
00:12:55,175 --> 00:12:56,176
Embarrassing?

183
00:12:56,243 --> 00:12:57,544
Come on, no way.

184
00:12:57,945 --> 00:12:59,413
What do you mean, no way?

185
00:13:00,314 --> 00:13:01,281
In that book,

186
00:13:02,583 --> 00:13:05,586
before releasing the moon bear,
in hopes that he'd adapt well,

187
00:13:06,153 --> 00:13:08,889
they teach him to hunt and don't let him
get close to humans,

188
00:13:08,889 --> 00:13:11,925
and the zoo staff even keep their
distance on purpose, right?

189
00:13:12,492 --> 00:13:16,363
But Star secretly brings him food,

190
00:13:16,697 --> 00:13:19,867
pets him more, and even sleeps
next to him.

191
00:13:21,201 --> 00:13:22,169
That's right.

192
00:13:22,536 --> 00:13:24,838
Then a senior zookeeper catches her,

193
00:13:25,439 --> 00:13:26,607
"You're fired!"

194
00:13:27,908 --> 00:13:29,309
And that's where Book 2 ends!

195
00:13:30,635 --> 00:13:32,646
Isn't Kkong Kkong
a master of cliffhangers?

196
00:13:36,617 --> 00:13:38,151
I've always been curious.

197
00:13:39,553 --> 00:13:42,289
Whether Star really got fired,

198
00:13:43,257 --> 00:13:46,426
and whether Half Moon is doing well
after leaving the zoo.

199
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:51,765
You want me to tell you
what happens to Star?

200
00:13:51,765 --> 00:13:53,233
No, no!

201
00:13:53,233 --> 00:13:56,203
Never! Don't spoil it for me.
I'm going to read the book.

202
00:14:02,709 --> 00:14:04,811
So I have a question.

203
00:14:05,679 --> 00:14:10,050
You said you found a lot of comfort
in "Star and the Half Moon" before.

204
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,921
I did.

205
00:14:20,594 --> 00:14:23,096
He lost his touch after military service.

206
00:14:23,163 --> 00:14:24,932
He never really had it.

207
00:14:25,098 --> 00:14:28,202
Tak Mu I's acting always seems so fake.
Don't you think?

208
00:14:28,435 --> 00:14:29,536
You know what I mean?

209
00:14:29,937 --> 00:14:31,572
Forget what it was before the military.

210
00:14:31,572 --> 00:14:33,974
Now that he's back,
his acting has to be up to par.

211
00:14:34,274 --> 00:14:36,343
- Considering how much he's paid!
- Exactly.

212
00:14:36,677 --> 00:14:38,145
Does he think he's still a child actor?

213
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:43,617
I was so scared at the time
that I decided to run away from it all.

214
00:14:44,017 --> 00:14:47,187
- What could I do besides acting?
- Okay, you're good. Go.

215
00:14:47,187 --> 00:14:48,655
- Go, go.
- I wanted to find out.

216
00:14:53,527 --> 00:14:54,561
Hello.

217
00:14:57,064 --> 00:14:58,065
Palms.

218
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,000
- What?
- Show me your palms.

219
00:15:01,635 --> 00:15:03,237
Come on, take off your gloves.

220
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,207
Flip them over.

221
00:15:09,343 --> 00:15:10,944
Unbelievable.

222
00:15:11,278 --> 00:15:13,280
We can't hire people
with hands like yours.

223
00:15:13,514 --> 00:15:16,717
Everyone here has cheated death
more than once.

224
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:20,053
One slip can kill us,
and so can awkward amateurs like you.

225
00:15:20,821 --> 00:15:23,690
Looks like you came
for some "life experience" type of thing.

226
00:15:23,690 --> 00:15:24,925
Go find it somewhere else.

227
00:15:27,327 --> 00:15:30,731
But the outside world wasn't exactly easy.

228
00:15:30,731 --> 00:15:32,666
(Hadong-ri)

229
00:15:32,666 --> 00:15:34,434
I was about to give up and go back,

230
00:15:35,502 --> 00:15:36,470
when in that book,

231
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:37,471
("Star and the Half Moon 1")

232
00:15:37,471 --> 00:15:41,074
the things Star says to the moon bear
when he's leaving the zoo,

233
00:15:41,742 --> 00:15:43,377
felt like they were all meant for me.

234
00:15:45,145 --> 00:15:47,381
So I mustered up the courage once more.

235
00:15:49,216 --> 00:15:53,854
After a year and a half out in the world,
rubbing shoulders with people,

236
00:15:54,755 --> 00:15:56,356
I wanted to act again.

237
00:15:57,691 --> 00:16:01,428
So do you know why the author
Kkong Kkong doesn't write anymore?

238
00:16:05,866 --> 00:16:06,867
Who knows?

239
00:16:23,717 --> 00:16:25,886
I'll be fine. I can go on my own.

240
00:16:27,855 --> 00:16:31,725
Well, even if you won't lend me Book 3,
you'll need to give my books back, right?

241
00:16:31,725 --> 00:16:33,026
("Star and the Half Moon 1")

242
00:16:37,598 --> 00:16:38,632
Let's go up together.

243
00:16:38,699 --> 00:16:40,968
No, it's not like I can't walk.

244
00:16:41,668 --> 00:16:44,671
Thank you so much for the shoes.
I appreciate it.

245
00:16:46,507 --> 00:16:48,375
Goodbye.

246
00:17:25,212 --> 00:17:26,180
Hey, Yeong Su.

247
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,882
So she just has to pay a fine?

248
00:17:30,425 --> 00:17:31,393
Well, that's too bad.

249
00:17:31,417 --> 00:17:32,419
What can we do?

250
00:17:34,021 --> 00:17:36,023
Okay, get home safely.

251
00:17:36,924 --> 00:17:37,891
All right.

252
00:17:42,863 --> 00:17:43,897
Excuse me!

253
00:17:47,935 --> 00:17:49,169
What is it? What's going on?

254
00:17:50,037 --> 00:17:52,573
I'll lend you this.

255
00:17:56,677 --> 00:17:58,011
("Star and the Half Moon 3")

256
00:18:01,548 --> 00:18:02,850
Thank you so much!

257
00:18:03,083 --> 00:18:04,885
I'll treasure it. I really will!

258
00:18:06,019 --> 00:18:08,922
I'm so happy right now
my heart could burst.

259
00:18:16,363 --> 00:18:18,799
Thank you, truly. I'll be careful with it.

260
00:18:33,447 --> 00:18:35,716
("Star and the Half Moon 3")

261
00:19:05,946 --> 00:19:07,581
Hey, you scared me!

262
00:19:09,316 --> 00:19:10,284
What time is it?

263
00:19:10,951 --> 00:19:11,919
It's 11.

264
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:13,921
Did you sleep?

265
00:19:13,921 --> 00:19:14,888
At what time?

266
00:19:15,622 --> 00:19:16,693
I don't know.

267
00:19:16,717 --> 00:19:18,625
I think I fell asleep
after sunrise.

268
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:21,962
The sun comes up at 6 these days.

269
00:19:22,809 --> 00:19:23,997
You slept five whole hours?

270
00:19:29,336 --> 00:19:31,939
Hey! You finally got it!

271
00:19:33,292 --> 00:19:35,542
She only caved after she got hurt
because of you?

272
00:19:36,043 --> 00:19:38,979
I don't get it, but how awesome is
Gong Yu Il, seriously?

273
00:19:40,681 --> 00:19:44,318
I'm suddenly starting to feel
grateful to Song Yun O.

274
00:19:44,318 --> 00:19:45,686
All right, yay for everyone.

275
00:19:46,887 --> 00:19:48,689
Let's go. We have to get to the screening.

276
00:19:50,457 --> 00:19:53,927
Hey, what took you so long?
There, there, aren't you pretty?

277
00:19:54,261 --> 00:19:55,429
Seriously!

278
00:19:56,897 --> 00:19:58,732
What are you doing? That's so gross.

279
00:20:00,067 --> 00:20:01,034
Darn it.

280
00:20:01,969 --> 00:20:08,509
("I Didn't Know Then" to 10 Mil!)

281
00:20:09,176 --> 00:20:10,210
Will you be okay?

282
00:20:10,611 --> 00:20:12,613
If it's too much, we can do it ourselves.

283
00:20:12,646 --> 00:20:13,780
No, no. I'm fine.

284
00:20:15,148 --> 00:20:16,517
Can you tell I'm sweating?

285
00:20:19,686 --> 00:20:20,654
Water?

286
00:20:20,888 --> 00:20:21,855
- Thanks.
- Sure.

287
00:20:26,326 --> 00:20:28,095
Cast members, please make your entrance.

288
00:20:29,663 --> 00:20:30,963
Hey, are you okay?

289
00:20:36,136 --> 00:20:38,572
Yeah, I'm fine.

290
00:20:42,376 --> 00:20:43,877
("I Didn't Know Then")

291
00:20:44,011 --> 00:20:46,046
(Now Showing to Acclaim)

292
00:20:46,079 --> 00:20:47,781
("I Didn't Know Then")

293
00:21:13,607 --> 00:21:14,908
It's all about mindset.

294
00:21:16,443 --> 00:21:17,444
Don't be scared.

295
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:20,948
Let's go!

296
00:21:50,110 --> 00:21:51,378
(Tak Mu I, Rooting for you!)

297
00:22:04,525 --> 00:22:05,526
Michael Jackson?

298
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:09,863
("I Didn't Know Then" Smash Hit!
"I Didn't Know Then" to 10 Mil!)

299
00:22:09,897 --> 00:22:11,532
("I Didn't Know Then")

300
00:22:19,873 --> 00:22:21,041
Hello.

301
00:22:25,145 --> 00:22:26,713
(Gangseong General Hospital)

302
00:22:29,082 --> 00:22:30,083
Goodness.

303
00:22:32,186 --> 00:22:34,188
You guys couldn't get a room
somewhere else?

304
00:22:35,616 --> 00:22:37,024
You had to make it weird.

305
00:22:37,424 --> 00:22:40,661
Then should we rehearse at his agency,
where fans are camped out?

306
00:22:41,295 --> 00:22:42,429
Or should we go to my place?

307
00:22:43,197 --> 00:22:46,200
We can't do it at a café, and there are
plenty of empty rooms here.

308
00:22:46,834 --> 00:22:49,736
Fine, that explains you two,
but what about you?

309
00:22:50,003 --> 00:22:51,905
I came to buy these guys some food.

310
00:22:52,973 --> 00:22:53,941
Here.

311
00:22:55,042 --> 00:22:56,009
Eat up.

312
00:23:02,783 --> 00:23:04,418
Wait, you have to put this in too.

313
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:07,921
Try some.

314
00:23:09,356 --> 00:23:11,525
Mu I, why are you acting so weird?

315
00:23:12,059 --> 00:23:13,493
This isn't like you at all.

316
00:23:15,295 --> 00:23:17,231
Hey, you got something on your shirt.

317
00:23:17,898 --> 00:23:19,666
What? When did this…

318
00:23:20,601 --> 00:23:21,602
I need the restroom.

319
00:23:21,602 --> 00:23:22,769
Yeah, go ahead.

320
00:23:24,137 --> 00:23:25,105
Is it good?

321
00:23:25,606 --> 00:23:27,274
Mu I, you have something to say?

322
00:23:28,208 --> 00:23:29,543
Feel free to just say it.

323
00:23:33,747 --> 00:23:35,148
I have a favor to ask.

324
00:23:35,716 --> 00:23:37,618
You're a guest with Ian Kim's band, right?

325
00:23:38,418 --> 00:23:39,386
Yes.

326
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:41,355
I can't find tickets no matter how I try.

327
00:23:43,624 --> 00:23:44,811
That's what this is about?

328
00:23:45,312 --> 00:23:47,027
Why is that so difficult to ask?

329
00:23:47,494 --> 00:23:48,529
How many do you need?

330
00:23:49,363 --> 00:23:50,364
Two.

331
00:23:50,797 --> 00:23:53,000
Hey, please don't tell Da Hong…

332
00:23:54,468 --> 00:23:55,502
What's going on?

333
00:23:55,836 --> 00:23:57,604
Why did you stop talking when I came?

334
00:23:59,072 --> 00:24:01,508
Without our Da Hong,
the conversation keeps dying.

335
00:24:02,109 --> 00:24:03,143
You silly.

336
00:24:04,411 --> 00:24:05,546
I should get going.

337
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,447
It's almost time for practice.

338
00:24:07,781 --> 00:24:09,483
Okay, go ahead.

339
00:24:09,783 --> 00:24:11,585
Now Mu I and I can make this a date.

340
00:24:13,287 --> 00:24:14,888
- I'll call you.
- Yeah, go on.

341
00:24:16,123 --> 00:24:17,324
Bye.

342
00:24:21,862 --> 00:24:23,797
(Sobaek Gukbap)

343
00:24:27,501 --> 00:24:28,602
- Da Hong.
- Yeah?

344
00:24:29,703 --> 00:24:31,371
Stop looking at me and eat.

345
00:24:33,307 --> 00:24:36,543
It makes me happy, just watching you eat,
even if I don't take a bite.

346
00:24:37,010 --> 00:24:38,545
It's my favorite way to diet.

347
00:24:46,253 --> 00:24:49,389
- Hey, Min left his phone.
- Yeah, you're right.

348
00:24:49,990 --> 00:24:51,692
I'll give this to him. Keep eating.

349
00:24:51,692 --> 00:24:52,693
Okay, go ahead.

350
00:24:56,029 --> 00:24:57,617
Hey, Min, your phone!

351
00:25:10,544 --> 00:25:12,179
(Pregnancy to Birth Care, Rion OB-GYN)

352
00:25:17,684 --> 00:25:19,520
Hey, I was so startled I spat.

353
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:22,589
If I chipped my tooth,
I couldn't have been on set today.

354
00:25:22,756 --> 00:25:23,991
I was startled too.

355
00:25:24,725 --> 00:25:26,360
Don't leave your phone behind.

356
00:25:26,894 --> 00:25:28,262
- Thanks. I'll see you.
- Yeah.

357
00:25:28,395 --> 00:25:29,396
Bye.

358
00:25:32,344 --> 00:25:34,601
Da Hong is so wrong for him.

359
00:25:34,902 --> 00:25:36,637
It might not even be true,

360
00:25:37,271 --> 00:25:40,407
and even if those two are dating,
why would your world collapse?

361
00:25:41,808 --> 00:25:44,011
Please, let's just live in reality, okay?

362
00:25:45,012 --> 00:25:46,180
I'm busy. Bye.

363
00:25:50,972 --> 00:25:52,319
These two?

364
00:25:53,053 --> 00:25:54,688
I don't think so…

365
00:25:54,721 --> 00:25:56,423
(Fans Shocked by Background Image
of Singer Ryu Min & Joo Da Hong!)

366
00:26:00,494 --> 00:26:03,397
The background does make it awkward…

367
00:26:05,627 --> 00:26:07,134
That's an uncanny background.

368
00:26:07,935 --> 00:26:10,304
- How did you do it?
- What else is there?

369
00:26:10,771 --> 00:26:13,941
There's no other way.
You just have to put in the legwork.

370
00:26:15,175 --> 00:26:17,462
Well, we have two reporters named Park.

371
00:26:17,529 --> 00:26:18,745
One hits the jackpot,

372
00:26:19,546 --> 00:26:21,682
and the other never has any luck.

373
00:26:40,968 --> 00:26:41,969
Can I help you?

374
00:26:43,770 --> 00:26:46,773
Did you take that photo on site yourself?

375
00:26:47,241 --> 00:26:48,509
You used your phone, right?

376
00:26:48,675 --> 00:26:51,678
Who runs on foot these days?
We run with our fingers.

377
00:26:52,646 --> 00:26:56,517
Hey, in this immense flood of information,

378
00:26:56,884 --> 00:27:01,563
picking out the real catch means
you have a sharp, trendy sensibility.

379
00:27:05,192 --> 00:27:06,994
How long will you keep phoning it in?

380
00:27:07,394 --> 00:27:09,096
Who says I'm phoning it in?

381
00:27:09,496 --> 00:27:11,598
I'm not phoning it in.
I'm collecting my dues.

382
00:27:13,433 --> 00:27:14,668
Did you fact-check it?

383
00:27:15,002 --> 00:27:17,671
I've followed Ryu Min for months.

384
00:27:17,671 --> 00:27:19,339
I never found anything on him, but…

385
00:27:19,339 --> 00:27:22,309
You claim to fact-check
without stating a single fact,

386
00:27:22,976 --> 00:27:26,013
and honestly, whether it's true or not
doesn't matter,

387
00:27:26,713 --> 00:27:27,915
as long as it's fun.

388
00:27:28,148 --> 00:27:29,950
But it's news, and we're reporters…

389
00:27:29,950 --> 00:27:30,953
Listen to me.

390
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:34,388
These days in the world that we live in,
news is entertainment too.

391
00:27:35,122 --> 00:27:37,758
Reporter Park-over-yonder, got it?

392
00:27:38,825 --> 00:27:40,994
Also, you may as well drink hot coffee.

393
00:27:41,628 --> 00:27:44,131
Then maybe something hot
will fall on your lap.

394
00:27:49,670 --> 00:27:51,438
(Fans Shocked by Background Image
of Singer Ryu Min & Joo Da Hong!)

395
00:27:52,773 --> 00:27:54,975
I kept my phone away last night,
so I had no clue.

396
00:27:56,443 --> 00:27:58,045
Should I tell the press I was there?

397
00:27:59,146 --> 00:28:01,315
Reporters called, so I already told them.

398
00:28:02,149 --> 00:28:03,183
Good job.

399
00:28:04,952 --> 00:28:05,953
Aside from Ryu Min,

400
00:28:06,653 --> 00:28:08,455
I wonder if Da Hong is okay.

401
00:28:09,056 --> 00:28:11,191
I called Da Hong because I was worried,

402
00:28:11,992 --> 00:28:12,960
and she said,

403
00:28:14,094 --> 00:28:17,698
"Whatever reporter bastards did this,
if I get my hands on them,

404
00:28:17,831 --> 00:28:23,470
I'll rip their heads off
and tear them limb from limb!"

405
00:28:25,639 --> 00:28:28,475
She got all worked up
like that on her own and hung up.

406
00:28:28,775 --> 00:28:30,277
She might talk that way to you,

407
00:28:30,811 --> 00:28:32,546
but then she might be crying in secret.

408
00:28:34,915 --> 00:28:37,651
Why should I explain myself?
I've got nothing to explain.

409
00:28:38,552 --> 00:28:39,520
Is it really not true?

410
00:28:39,553 --> 00:28:42,422
This is so annoying. I just told you!

411
00:28:42,623 --> 00:28:44,091
Soup, phone, spit!

412
00:28:44,758 --> 00:28:46,593
This isn't even worthy of the tabloids.

413
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:49,863
Who do you think makes
tabloid stories sound credible?

414
00:28:50,030 --> 00:28:51,797
You're getting old, Mr. CEO.

415
00:28:51,821 --> 00:28:53,734
Who panics over dating rumors these days?

416
00:28:53,734 --> 00:28:55,669
It's because the other party is Ryu Min!

417
00:28:55,936 --> 00:28:58,138
They'll think you seduced him first!

418
00:28:59,806 --> 00:29:01,542
Whatever, I'm leaving. I have a shoot.

419
00:29:02,075 --> 00:29:04,077
Don't call me in for this ever again!

420
00:29:05,179 --> 00:29:08,682
Like mother, like daughter,
already running around seducing men.

421
00:29:10,684 --> 00:29:11,910
Exactly.

422
00:29:11,977 --> 00:29:13,654
I am the CEO's daughter after all.

423
00:29:14,388 --> 00:29:15,355
Right, Dad?

424
00:29:20,993 --> 00:29:23,230
This is karma. It's karma.

425
00:29:26,697 --> 00:29:27,698
That little…

426
00:29:34,241 --> 00:29:35,375
Hello, Da Hong.

427
00:29:37,644 --> 00:29:40,814
I made it clear to you
that this is my seat.

428
00:29:43,383 --> 00:29:45,285
Ma'am, this way, please.

429
00:30:00,934 --> 00:30:04,972
Well, since she even brought down Ryu Min,
who's famous for being unapproachable,

430
00:30:05,439 --> 00:30:08,976
winning over salon staff
must be a piece of cake.

431
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:11,745
Is that hereditary or what?

432
00:30:12,112 --> 00:30:13,547
What did you just say?

433
00:30:16,316 --> 00:30:19,553
That you're good at seducing people
like your mom.

434
00:30:20,787 --> 00:30:21,755
It's a compliment.

435
00:30:25,626 --> 00:30:28,328
Hey, you heard what she said too, right?

436
00:30:29,296 --> 00:30:31,265
She landed the first blow
with a jab at my family,

437
00:30:31,698 --> 00:30:33,367
so now it's self-defense, you wench!

438
00:30:33,367 --> 00:30:34,835
- Hey, get up!
- Let go of me!

439
00:30:35,269 --> 00:30:36,570
Say it again, say it again.

440
00:30:37,838 --> 00:30:39,139
- Calm down.
- I said let go!

441
00:30:44,144 --> 00:30:45,212
Are you insane?

442
00:30:45,979 --> 00:30:47,481
Fine, hit me, hit me.

443
00:31:03,263 --> 00:31:04,264
Hey!

444
00:31:04,331 --> 00:31:06,867
What do you think you're doing?

445
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:12,673
What if people see you?

446
00:31:13,540 --> 00:31:15,576
You'll never be at my level, ever.

447
00:31:15,609 --> 00:31:18,178
Just admit it
and take the roles I turn down.

448
00:31:18,645 --> 00:31:19,613
Hey.

449
00:31:19,613 --> 00:31:21,849
Why did you bring that up again,
you mean wench?

450
00:31:21,849 --> 00:31:22,816
What? Wench?

451
00:31:22,916 --> 00:31:24,585
Hey, stop, stop!

452
00:31:25,819 --> 00:31:27,154
Cut it out, Joo Da Hong!

453
00:31:27,454 --> 00:31:29,279
What if your father finds out?

454
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:32,392
The customers are all watching,
and if someone records you,

455
00:31:32,893 --> 00:31:37,097
do you not care about your image
or dignity as an actress?

456
00:31:37,164 --> 00:31:38,298
Dignity?

457
00:31:38,765 --> 00:31:40,334
Screw that! Hey, get over here!

458
00:31:40,434 --> 00:31:42,035
Hey, stop!

459
00:31:43,837 --> 00:31:45,105
Stop it!

460
00:31:49,276 --> 00:31:51,578
(Will be back after a restroom break)

461
00:31:54,147 --> 00:31:56,383
- Hey, did you guys see it yesterday?
- What?

462
00:31:56,383 --> 00:31:58,819
Why were Ryu Min and Joo Da Hong
photographed in a place like that?

463
00:31:58,819 --> 00:32:00,554
- Why, what about it?
- That's so ugly.

464
00:32:00,554 --> 00:32:02,556
- When are you going on a diet?
- That's really insulting.

465
00:32:02,556 --> 00:32:04,525
- Diet starts tomorrow.
- Sorry.

466
00:32:05,325 --> 00:32:06,260
Would you like a bag?

467
00:32:06,593 --> 00:32:08,262
No, we're eating here.

468
00:32:12,366 --> 00:32:15,202
- This is so good.
- Hey, this is really good. Try it.

469
00:32:15,235 --> 00:32:16,870
- I want a bite too.
- Hey, you're spilling.

470
00:32:16,870 --> 00:32:17,905
Hey, you can't hand it over like that.

471
00:32:17,972 --> 00:32:19,840
Dang it. This is so frustrating.

472
00:32:21,141 --> 00:32:22,876
Please, please.

473
00:32:23,443 --> 00:32:25,012
Hey, so are you going if they come?

474
00:32:25,079 --> 00:32:26,046
- Well…
- Let's go.

475
00:32:26,046 --> 00:32:27,414
- I suddenly don't want to go.
- Can't you go with her?

476
00:32:27,414 --> 00:32:29,216
- I said let's go.
- Even better.

477
00:32:29,716 --> 00:32:31,518
- I'm so full.
- Hey, let's go now.

478
00:32:31,518 --> 00:32:32,753
Let's clean up and go.

479
00:32:33,253 --> 00:32:34,288
Just leave it!

480
00:32:34,621 --> 00:32:35,589
I'll clean it up.

481
00:32:35,589 --> 00:32:38,592
- Wait, are you serious?
- Thank you, ma'am.

482
00:32:38,592 --> 00:32:39,993
- Let's hurry.
- Goodbye!

483
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,361
Take care.

484
00:32:46,466 --> 00:32:47,901
Ma'am!

485
00:32:47,901 --> 00:32:49,236
- Hey, open the door!
- Goodness.

486
00:32:49,236 --> 00:32:50,270
Ma'am!

487
00:32:50,871 --> 00:32:53,607
Hey, can I exchange this? It all melted.

488
00:32:54,641 --> 00:32:55,776
I can't.

489
00:32:56,076 --> 00:32:59,379
Come on, just this once.
I haven't even opened it.

490
00:32:59,947 --> 00:33:03,283
Even if it isn't opened,
if it can't be resold,

491
00:33:03,308 --> 00:33:06,503
- I can't exchange it, okay?
- Come on, please.

492
00:33:06,528 --> 00:33:07,955
I'm only a student!

493
00:33:07,955 --> 00:33:09,656
$1.50 is a lot for a student.

494
00:33:09,923 --> 00:33:13,293
Why are you doing this to me?
What, are you a Tak Mu I fan?

495
00:33:14,027 --> 00:33:15,929
What? Why did you bring up Tak Mu I?

496
00:33:16,763 --> 00:33:18,632
Anyway, I can't.

497
00:33:18,866 --> 00:33:21,235
You should've bought it
after you finished your ramyeon.

498
00:33:21,668 --> 00:33:23,971
Then you should've told us beforehand.

499
00:33:24,605 --> 00:33:26,740
You're so darn picky for a part-timer.

500
00:33:27,674 --> 00:33:28,642
What?

501
00:33:29,576 --> 00:33:32,446
Young lady, what did you just say?

502
00:33:32,946 --> 00:33:35,349
- "For a part-timer"?
- I never said that.

503
00:33:39,620 --> 00:33:40,754
- Welcome…
- Hello.

504
00:33:44,625 --> 00:33:47,294
- You work here too?
- Yes.

505
00:33:49,796 --> 00:33:53,000
I'm in a bit of a hurry, so could you
cover the counter for a moment…

506
00:33:55,502 --> 00:33:57,171
And don't allow this girl to exchange.

507
00:33:58,872 --> 00:33:59,907
No, I…

508
00:34:08,691 --> 00:34:09,696
Thank goodness.

509
00:34:13,017 --> 00:34:15,055
Of all times, my goodness…

510
00:34:22,529 --> 00:34:23,564
I'm sorry.

511
00:34:23,564 --> 00:34:26,567
I had a very urgent, important call.

512
00:34:34,557 --> 00:34:35,561
Okay.

513
00:34:37,978 --> 00:34:39,179
So did that girl leave?

514
00:34:40,047 --> 00:34:41,215
Well…

515
00:34:41,215 --> 00:34:44,318
Well, she didn't just walk out on her own.
I gave a reason to leave.

516
00:34:45,485 --> 00:34:46,486
Sorry?

517
00:34:48,455 --> 00:34:49,423
Take a new one.

518
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:52,826
Really? Handsome guys really are
easier to talk to.

519
00:34:52,826 --> 00:34:53,994
Actually,

520
00:34:55,629 --> 00:34:57,698
I saw it all while I was parking earlier.

521
00:34:59,099 --> 00:35:01,168
You know e-cigs are cigarettes too, right?

522
00:35:02,035 --> 00:35:05,205
School, police station, home,

523
00:35:06,440 --> 00:35:09,610
which call would be the biggest hassle
to make you quit smoking?

524
00:35:10,878 --> 00:35:12,045
Do you have proof?

525
00:35:14,214 --> 00:35:15,782
See the security camera out there?

526
00:35:16,583 --> 00:35:19,686
Also, my car's dashcam
probably caught it too.

527
00:35:26,693 --> 00:35:30,898
Never bother this store clerk again,

528
00:35:31,932 --> 00:35:35,269
and don't get flirty with random people.

529
00:35:36,036 --> 00:35:38,405
No after-meal smokes
and no skipping class.

530
00:35:40,841 --> 00:35:42,009
You understand me?

531
00:35:49,850 --> 00:35:50,817
Thank you.

532
00:35:52,819 --> 00:35:56,657
By the way, that day I brought coffee,

533
00:35:56,657 --> 00:35:57,702
but you'd left.

534
00:35:57,726 --> 00:35:59,760
You weren't at the Kids Café
Cooking Booth either.

535
00:36:01,507 --> 00:36:03,063
So you did come back.

536
00:36:03,711 --> 00:36:06,414
If I'd known, I wouldn't have gone back
to the restaurant so soon.

537
00:36:07,835 --> 00:36:10,037
- The restaurant?
- Yes.

538
00:36:13,640 --> 00:36:15,642
I'm actually a chef.

539
00:36:15,776 --> 00:36:17,444
I'm not employed at the kids' café.

540
00:36:19,313 --> 00:36:23,317
So you actually work at a restaurant.

541
00:36:23,550 --> 00:36:25,185
I had no idea.

542
00:36:27,321 --> 00:36:30,190
Wait, that's all you're eating for lunch?

543
00:36:31,024 --> 00:36:32,259
Yeah, well.

544
00:36:33,260 --> 00:36:36,163
When you cook for a living,
you don't have time or the appetite.

545
00:36:38,632 --> 00:36:39,600
Just a moment.

546
00:36:42,569 --> 00:36:44,371
Take some coffee with you too.

547
00:36:45,439 --> 00:36:47,608
This one's on me,
the one I couldn't give you then.

548
00:36:47,708 --> 00:36:48,742
Thanks.

549
00:36:51,445 --> 00:36:52,913
Want to work together?

550
00:36:53,881 --> 00:36:55,949
I heard the restaurant needs floor staff.

551
00:36:57,351 --> 00:36:58,352
What?

552
00:36:58,519 --> 00:36:59,987
Like you said the other day,

553
00:37:00,254 --> 00:37:03,123
food is like the medicine
that heals the heart.

554
00:37:03,290 --> 00:37:04,324
It's quite similar.

555
00:37:08,195 --> 00:37:12,332
Unfortunately, this place
wouldn't run without me.

556
00:37:12,766 --> 00:37:14,334
I've worked here for a long time,

557
00:37:14,668 --> 00:37:18,639
and my boss probably won't let me go.

558
00:37:20,172 --> 00:37:21,575
Sorry. Am I late?

559
00:37:21,575 --> 00:37:22,709
- Hi there.
- Hey.

560
00:37:23,544 --> 00:37:24,578
Goodness.

561
00:37:28,682 --> 00:37:29,650
Yu Il,

562
00:37:32,719 --> 00:37:34,021
how do I say this?

563
00:37:36,890 --> 00:37:39,793
- I can't keep you around anymore.
- What?

564
00:37:39,993 --> 00:37:43,797
With a baby on the way,
plenty of expenses,

565
00:37:44,398 --> 00:37:46,667
and my freeloading brother to deal with,

566
00:37:47,067 --> 00:37:49,670
my brother and I will run the store
instead of hiring part-timers.

567
00:37:50,838 --> 00:37:52,272
Anyway, I'm sorry about this, okay?

568
00:37:52,506 --> 00:37:54,041
I'm going to the storeroom.
Start tidying up.

569
00:37:54,041 --> 00:37:55,008
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

570
00:38:02,115 --> 00:38:04,418
- Give me your phone.
- What?

571
00:38:04,451 --> 00:38:05,452
It'll just take a second.

572
00:38:14,094 --> 00:38:16,263
It's here. Think about it.

573
00:38:16,730 --> 00:38:17,764
And also…

574
00:38:18,732 --> 00:38:19,766
thanks for the coffee.

575
00:38:20,968 --> 00:38:22,870
Okay, take care.

576
00:38:29,076 --> 00:38:32,079
He works at a really famous restaurant.

577
00:39:16,557 --> 00:39:18,592
"Sorry for visiting when you weren't home.

578
00:39:18,992 --> 00:39:21,128
"Just in case, make sure to put it on.

579
00:39:21,862 --> 00:39:22,863
"Tak Mu I"

580
00:39:29,236 --> 00:39:30,404
He bought so much.

581
00:39:46,486 --> 00:39:48,021
(Min Ye tagged Da Hong in a post)

582
00:39:48,055 --> 00:39:49,022
What's this?

583
00:39:54,161 --> 00:39:56,096
(Da Hong, whom I met at the salon,
always confident, unbothered by others.)

584
00:39:56,096 --> 00:39:58,098
(I support both your love and your work!
Joo Da Hong, you look so confident!)

585
00:39:58,098 --> 00:40:00,100
(You're so pretty, Min Ye,
You're way prettier.)

586
00:40:00,100 --> 00:40:01,101
(My goddess.)

587
00:40:01,101 --> 00:40:03,804
(Min Ye is way better than Joo Da Hong!)

588
00:40:03,804 --> 00:40:05,806
(Joo Da Hong is meh,
Kang Min Ye has so many followers.)

589
00:40:05,806 --> 00:40:07,808
(I always watch your YouTube!
I love you, Kang Min Ye.)

590
00:40:07,808 --> 00:40:10,043
(Are you not filming a TV show?
Isn't Kang Min Ye a bad actress?)

591
00:40:10,043 --> 00:40:11,211
(Joo Da Hong is worse.)

592
00:40:11,278 --> 00:40:13,046
So I didn't rip out enough of her hair!

593
00:40:15,082 --> 00:40:17,117
So that's how she's playing it?

594
00:40:21,221 --> 00:40:22,189
(LIVE)

595
00:40:22,189 --> 00:40:23,857
Hi, everyone!

596
00:40:24,191 --> 00:40:26,326
Hongajis, have you been well?

597
00:40:26,460 --> 00:40:29,429
It's been a while since my last live.
I know you've been patient.

598
00:40:29,429 --> 00:40:31,398
So I'm here to tell you myself.

599
00:40:32,733 --> 00:40:35,669
I'm not dating Ryu Min.

600
00:40:36,970 --> 00:40:39,306
I'm not dating him.

601
00:40:41,708 --> 00:40:45,579
Maybe it's because Min Ye is in such
a beautiful relationship herself,

602
00:40:45,579 --> 00:40:47,147
that she thought I was too.

603
00:40:47,548 --> 00:40:52,386
They say people in love believe that
everyone else is experiencing love too.

604
00:40:54,955 --> 00:40:57,157
This crazy wench!

605
00:40:58,492 --> 00:41:01,795
You probably read that I had lunch
with my fellow cast members that day.

606
00:41:02,930 --> 00:41:04,198
Don't believe me?

607
00:41:04,531 --> 00:41:08,235
If you don't, go to that gukbap place
and check the security footage.

608
00:41:10,637 --> 00:41:13,607
Sadly, I'm not seeing anyone right now,

609
00:41:14,308 --> 00:41:16,710
but should I tell just my beloved Hongajis
a secret?

610
00:41:17,644 --> 00:41:20,914
Actually, there's someone I like.

611
00:41:22,916 --> 00:41:23,951
Who is it?

612
00:41:25,366 --> 00:41:26,753
Should I just say it?

613
00:41:27,654 --> 00:41:29,423
If I give you a little hint,

614
00:41:30,424 --> 00:41:33,393
the person I like is…

615
00:41:35,896 --> 00:41:38,565
What'd she say? What's this?
Joo Da Hong's done it now!

616
00:41:38,565 --> 00:41:39,600
Hey, look! Look!

617
00:41:40,601 --> 00:41:41,616
Hey!

618
00:41:44,538 --> 00:41:46,173
You have got to be kidding! Seriously?

619
00:41:47,608 --> 00:41:49,977
Yes, my first love.

620
00:41:50,410 --> 00:41:53,180
My first love is still ongoing.

621
00:41:54,181 --> 00:41:55,349
(Is Da Hong's Unrequited Love Tak Mu I?)

622
00:41:55,349 --> 00:41:56,350
(Past Remarks Resurface)

623
00:41:56,350 --> 00:41:59,586
They're even dredging up Da Hong's
old interviews, and it's going wild.

624
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:02,422
"Ryu Min is a smokescreen."
"These two must be an item."

625
00:42:02,890 --> 00:42:05,325
Ms. Kang, shouldn't we quickly put out
an explanation?

626
00:42:05,526 --> 00:42:06,493
I did.

627
00:42:06,960 --> 00:42:08,695
"We cannot confirm private matters."

628
00:42:09,329 --> 00:42:10,330
Ms. Kang!

629
00:42:10,564 --> 00:42:12,699
Mu I, look on the bright side.

630
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:15,235
This is exactly what viral marketing is.

631
00:42:15,903 --> 00:42:18,138
Joo Da Hong really is a pro.

632
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:21,341
("Rooftop Romance" Director)

633
00:42:22,843 --> 00:42:24,178
The "Rooftop Romance" director.

634
00:42:26,613 --> 00:42:28,148
Hello, Director.

635
00:42:30,017 --> 00:42:33,320
Yes, this is a good thing!
I was worried because his movie flopped.

636
00:42:33,787 --> 00:42:36,390
But just like that show where a woman
parachutes into North Korea,

637
00:42:36,723 --> 00:42:40,861
people will want to know if it's real,
so the ratings will certainly go way up.

638
00:42:41,495 --> 00:42:42,462
Yes.

639
00:42:43,130 --> 00:42:45,232
Yes, take care.

640
00:42:47,467 --> 00:42:49,903
It's all sorted. I must be a genius.

641
00:42:51,672 --> 00:42:52,739
All right!

642
00:42:59,913 --> 00:43:01,982
Mu I, use this opportunity.

643
00:43:03,133 --> 00:43:04,134
Even Grandma?

644
00:43:11,525 --> 00:43:12,826
(Mu I)

645
00:43:17,664 --> 00:43:19,867
Okay, fine, I'm sorry! I said I'm sorry!

646
00:43:20,234 --> 00:43:22,769
Who knew they'd dig up an interview
from when I was a kid?

647
00:43:22,769 --> 00:43:25,606
Of course, Joo Da Hong would
get mad at something she started.

648
00:43:25,873 --> 00:43:26,840
Hey, you!

649
00:43:26,840 --> 00:43:30,043
Everywhere I go, they ask
if I'm going to give you a chance.

650
00:43:30,143 --> 00:43:32,112
Good, I was curious about that too.

651
00:43:32,246 --> 00:43:34,181
- Hey!
- Why are you yelling?

652
00:43:34,181 --> 00:43:35,682
You're my first love. That's true.

653
00:43:35,749 --> 00:43:37,184
It's true, it's still ongoing!

654
00:43:37,484 --> 00:43:40,187
Is love a crime?
Is wanting my first love a crime?

655
00:43:40,554 --> 00:43:41,522
What on earth?

656
00:43:41,522 --> 00:43:43,790
Unrequited love? Don't be pathetic!
Get out here!

657
00:43:43,857 --> 00:43:46,426
- I have an interview to go to.
- I canceled it. Get out!

658
00:43:46,426 --> 00:43:48,428
- Dad, that hurts!
- Out, now!

659
00:43:48,428 --> 00:43:49,429
- Hey!
- Seriously!

660
00:43:49,429 --> 00:43:50,531
Go home, now!

661
00:43:52,165 --> 00:43:53,600
Unbelievable…

662
00:44:20,961 --> 00:44:22,429
(Yoo Yeon Ju)

663
00:44:22,429 --> 00:44:24,198
(Joo Da Hong's "Love for Tak Mu I"
Still One-Sided?)

664
00:44:26,567 --> 00:44:28,235
So it was unrequited love.

665
00:44:28,969 --> 00:44:30,237
Not mutual.

666
00:44:40,180 --> 00:44:42,616
Yu Il, it's Mom. I'm sick.

667
00:44:43,016 --> 00:44:44,384
I have a high fever.

668
00:44:44,751 --> 00:44:46,086
Can you stop by later?

669
00:44:50,057 --> 00:44:51,825
Yeah, I'll come by in the evening.

670
00:45:05,739 --> 00:45:07,341
I almost missed you.

671
00:45:07,508 --> 00:45:08,775
What brings you here?

672
00:45:10,110 --> 00:45:12,846
Well, that Da Hong article…

673
00:45:13,580 --> 00:45:15,482
Yeah, I saw it.

674
00:45:16,617 --> 00:45:17,718
You saw it.

675
00:45:18,519 --> 00:45:20,654
She's always joked around a bit…

676
00:45:22,789 --> 00:45:24,483
I didn't want you to get the wrong idea.

677
00:45:26,293 --> 00:45:28,462
It didn't seem like a joke.

678
00:45:29,463 --> 00:45:31,331
But what is there to misunderstand?

679
00:45:33,934 --> 00:45:34,935
Good point.

680
00:45:36,170 --> 00:45:37,404
What's there to misunderstand?

681
00:45:40,607 --> 00:45:42,309
Is that why you're here?

682
00:45:43,677 --> 00:45:44,711
No.

683
00:45:44,878 --> 00:45:46,547
I'm here to return the book.

684
00:45:48,949 --> 00:45:50,083
But…

685
00:45:51,752 --> 00:45:53,487
I forgot to bring the book.

686
00:45:54,955 --> 00:45:56,323
No rush, bring it when you can.

687
00:46:01,195 --> 00:46:02,262
Where are you going?

688
00:46:02,496 --> 00:46:04,164
Get in. I'll give you a ride.

689
00:46:04,631 --> 00:46:06,300
No, I can just take the bus.

690
00:46:08,001 --> 00:46:10,170
I'm going to miss the bus. I'll see you.

691
00:46:13,006 --> 00:46:14,374
Thanks for the medicine!

692
00:46:49,643 --> 00:46:51,011
- Hello.
- Hey.

693
00:46:51,612 --> 00:46:52,946
I'm here for the interview.

694
00:46:54,248 --> 00:46:57,150
You came early.
I heard the interview starts at half past.

695
00:46:57,684 --> 00:47:01,121
I came a bit earlier than the time
the manager gave me.

696
00:47:01,555 --> 00:47:02,890
Proving my diligence!

697
00:47:04,458 --> 00:47:06,793
- Why don't you sit here for now?
- Okay.

698
00:47:09,496 --> 00:47:12,165
But where is everyone else…

699
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:15,435
They went for a walk since it's nice out.

700
00:47:22,242 --> 00:47:25,078
How long have you worked here?

701
00:47:26,313 --> 00:47:29,316
Me? Since it opened.

702
00:47:32,177 --> 00:47:34,188
And you're still the rookie?

703
00:47:37,658 --> 00:47:41,094
If I join today, I'll definitely get you
out of the rookie spot.

704
00:47:45,199 --> 00:47:46,200
You sure about that?

705
00:47:46,667 --> 00:47:47,835
Well…

706
00:47:48,402 --> 00:47:52,439
If you gave me some interview tips,
my chances might go way up.

707
00:48:01,146 --> 00:48:02,416
Tips, you say?

708
00:48:05,786 --> 00:48:07,788
I heard the owner here is a chef.

709
00:48:08,422 --> 00:48:09,823
What's he like?

710
00:48:10,257 --> 00:48:12,025
I read some things online.

711
00:48:12,426 --> 00:48:17,130
People said that he seems
very strict and meticulous.

712
00:48:18,799 --> 00:48:19,800
For example?

713
00:48:21,535 --> 00:48:23,403
From a YouTube video I watched,

714
00:48:23,871 --> 00:48:25,205
the soup comes out, right?

715
00:48:25,606 --> 00:48:27,374
Someone came three times and measured,

716
00:48:27,374 --> 00:48:29,243
and the soup temperature was consistent.

717
00:48:29,376 --> 00:48:31,044
Even down to the decimal point.

718
00:48:32,379 --> 00:48:33,380
I got goosebumps.

719
00:48:34,381 --> 00:48:36,850
There was also a comment below.

720
00:48:37,885 --> 00:48:39,553
Is the owner there, by any chance,

721
00:48:39,820 --> 00:48:42,089
a kind of man who's thrilled
by perfect cooking.

722
00:48:42,789 --> 00:48:44,057
Like a total freak?

723
00:48:48,795 --> 00:48:50,464
He's not really like that, is he?

724
00:48:51,832 --> 00:48:54,368
Who knows, maybe he is.

725
00:48:57,771 --> 00:49:01,808
- Can I ask you something?
- Sure.

726
00:49:01,909 --> 00:49:04,878
Why did you decide to interview today?

727
00:49:05,345 --> 00:49:07,181
Was the timing just right to switch jobs?

728
00:49:09,650 --> 00:49:11,485
That too, but…

729
00:49:11,652 --> 00:49:16,123
you said food is similar to a medicine
that heals people's hearts,

730
00:49:16,757 --> 00:49:19,193
and that made me a little curious.

731
00:49:19,860 --> 00:49:22,462
What kind of food is sold here,

732
00:49:22,529 --> 00:49:24,932
what kind of people make it,

733
00:49:25,199 --> 00:49:27,868
and whether customers really get healed.

734
00:49:29,102 --> 00:49:31,939
But couldn't you find out as a customer?

735
00:49:31,972 --> 00:49:34,575
I'd never come here as a customer.

736
00:49:35,008 --> 00:49:35,976
Why not?

737
00:49:35,976 --> 00:49:39,112
They give you a snot-sized portion,
but it's so darn expensive.

738
00:49:39,112 --> 00:49:40,447
The waiting time is long, too.

739
00:49:41,748 --> 00:49:42,716
I'll give you that.

740
00:49:43,050 --> 00:49:44,985
I don't mean that's bad.

741
00:49:45,485 --> 00:49:48,822
Meaning it's a bit beyond my means?

742
00:49:54,695 --> 00:49:57,731
Well then, shall we begin the interview?

743
00:49:59,633 --> 00:50:00,634
What?

744
00:50:00,701 --> 00:50:02,970
I'm late introducing myself.

745
00:50:03,303 --> 00:50:05,105
I'm the owner-chef of "The Kitchen,"

746
00:50:05,672 --> 00:50:06,707
Kang Hee Su.

747
00:50:14,147 --> 00:50:15,215
Well, you know,

748
00:50:15,649 --> 00:50:19,586
that "man who's so thrilled
by perfect cooking."

749
00:50:19,953 --> 00:50:21,088
"Like a total freak."

750
00:50:30,764 --> 00:50:32,866
I suppose this is a good time
for me to walk out?

751
00:50:33,867 --> 00:50:36,370
Sure, if you want.

752
00:50:37,204 --> 00:50:38,372
I'm sorry.

753
00:50:43,377 --> 00:50:45,245
You'll start work next week.

754
00:50:46,547 --> 00:50:47,548
What?

755
00:50:57,491 --> 00:50:58,559
What was I thinking?

756
00:51:03,430 --> 00:51:06,366
Wait, why on earth did I get hired?

757
00:51:09,536 --> 00:51:10,737
Is he really a total freak?

758
00:51:15,809 --> 00:51:17,878
Mom, I'm getting on the bus now.

759
00:51:32,125 --> 00:51:33,093
Two people, please.

760
00:51:39,933 --> 00:51:44,004
See, CEO Joo had my manager
watch me and even take my phone.

761
00:51:44,171 --> 00:51:47,608
CEO Joo is both my dad
and the head of my agency…

762
00:51:47,841 --> 00:51:49,977
Wait, let me start
with why I'm basically grounded.

763
00:51:49,977 --> 00:51:51,645
I think I know.

764
00:51:53,213 --> 00:51:56,016
Anyway, I barely got my phone and left.

765
00:51:57,050 --> 00:52:00,654
I mean, I just left,
but I had nobody to call.

766
00:52:01,255 --> 00:52:04,858
I was wondering where to go
when I spotted you.

767
00:52:05,225 --> 00:52:06,793
So I just got on after you.

768
00:52:08,328 --> 00:52:10,163
But where are you going? Not home?

769
00:52:11,064 --> 00:52:12,833
To my mom's house.

770
00:52:13,967 --> 00:52:16,703
Wait, why are we acting
like we're besties?

771
00:52:20,407 --> 00:52:22,376
I just thought we might as well be.

772
00:52:22,709 --> 00:52:25,646
We already said we'd be like sisters,
so that makes us friends.

773
00:52:27,514 --> 00:52:28,549
Okay, fine.

774
00:52:29,750 --> 00:52:32,553
But where will you go when you get off?

775
00:52:33,187 --> 00:52:34,188
Me?

776
00:52:34,555 --> 00:52:35,889
I'm following you, of course.

777
00:52:43,830 --> 00:52:46,099
You're really coming along? To my house?

778
00:52:46,133 --> 00:52:47,134
Yeah.

779
00:52:47,234 --> 00:52:49,770
I have nowhere to go and no money now,

780
00:52:50,237 --> 00:52:52,206
and this isn't a neighborhood I know,

781
00:52:52,873 --> 00:52:55,108
and you're the only one I know.

782
00:52:55,576 --> 00:52:59,680
Still, why did you run away
from home so recklessly?

783
00:53:00,080 --> 00:53:02,516
Like I said, I'm not running away.
I've escaped.

784
00:53:02,649 --> 00:53:04,084
I really needed to leave quickly.

785
00:53:05,786 --> 00:53:06,954
Right now, I…

786
00:53:06,954 --> 00:53:10,791
feel like the plant in your window,
just being held up in the air, you know?

787
00:53:11,725 --> 00:53:13,794
Just let me stay with you, just for today.

788
00:53:14,494 --> 00:53:15,762
Please?

789
00:53:22,736 --> 00:53:23,737
Mom.

790
00:53:24,638 --> 00:53:25,706
Mom?

791
00:53:30,978 --> 00:53:32,045
Where did she go?

792
00:53:42,289 --> 00:53:44,024
This house looks like a TV show set.

793
00:53:45,192 --> 00:53:46,627
It is an old house.

794
00:53:47,194 --> 00:53:48,262
- Is this your room?
- Yeah.

795
00:53:53,218 --> 00:53:55,135
Why are there so many books?

796
00:53:58,272 --> 00:54:00,340
Wait, that's what Mu I was always reading.

797
00:54:00,874 --> 00:54:02,109
Sweetie, are you home?

798
00:54:04,378 --> 00:54:07,748
Mom, you said you were sick.
Where have you been?

799
00:54:08,148 --> 00:54:10,284
The salon. I felt a bit better.

800
00:54:10,817 --> 00:54:12,085
Do we have a guest?

801
00:54:12,886 --> 00:54:14,254
She looks like Joo Da Hong.

802
00:54:15,522 --> 00:54:18,458
Hello, I am Joo Da Hong…

803
00:54:18,992 --> 00:54:20,060
Well, here's the thing.

804
00:54:31,605 --> 00:54:33,540
- Let's talk.
- Let go.

805
00:54:33,540 --> 00:54:35,709
- It'll only take a minute.
- Talk about what?

806
00:54:36,276 --> 00:54:39,213
You left with your mistress
and ran two households.

807
00:54:39,646 --> 00:54:42,616
Why should I smile,
say "It's been so long" and eat with you?

808
00:54:43,116 --> 00:54:45,285
Should I ask how that woman's doing?

809
00:54:45,586 --> 00:54:48,255
Should I ask when you'll come again
and make plans with us?

810
00:54:50,224 --> 00:54:51,592
Don't ever do this again.

811
00:54:52,192 --> 00:54:55,629
- Next time, I won't see you either, Mom.
- Yu Il.

812
00:55:00,667 --> 00:55:01,702
Yu Il!

813
00:55:14,982 --> 00:55:17,251
I thought I'd finally get home cooking,

814
00:55:18,585 --> 00:55:19,553
Sorry.

815
00:55:20,687 --> 00:55:23,924
But it would've been awkward to sit there
and eat anyway.

816
00:55:24,658 --> 00:55:27,294
- What are you going to do now?
- I don't know.

817
00:55:27,728 --> 00:55:29,429
I don't want to go back there,

818
00:55:29,663 --> 00:55:32,299
but leaving like this doesn't feel right.

819
00:55:32,799 --> 00:55:33,834
Listen to yourself!

820
00:55:34,501 --> 00:55:36,970
Who runs away from home so recklessly?

821
00:55:37,905 --> 00:55:38,939
As you can see,

822
00:55:39,273 --> 00:55:42,943
it's not running away, it's an escape.
It was kind of urgent.

823
00:55:47,948 --> 00:55:49,416
You have it better than I do.

824
00:55:50,684 --> 00:55:52,819
My mom and dad both cheated on each other.

825
00:55:53,253 --> 00:55:55,455
They were with actors,
so the whole country knew.

826
00:55:56,490 --> 00:55:58,292
When the scandal with Ryu Min broke,

827
00:55:58,425 --> 00:56:00,661
someone said I'm good at seducing men
like my mom.

828
00:56:01,895 --> 00:56:02,963
Who?

829
00:56:03,163 --> 00:56:05,666
What awful person left
such a hateful comment?

830
00:56:06,066 --> 00:56:07,634
CEO Joo, my dad.

831
00:56:10,897 --> 00:56:13,232
It's fine. He is an awful man.

832
00:56:14,975 --> 00:56:15,943
Here.

833
00:56:19,546 --> 00:56:21,315
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

834
00:56:24,685 --> 00:56:29,823
If you're ever in pain,

835
00:56:31,258 --> 00:56:35,596
I'll comfort you

836
00:56:38,198 --> 00:56:39,967
How do you even know a song like that?

837
00:56:40,534 --> 00:56:45,172
If you're ever in pain,

838
00:56:46,773 --> 00:56:51,445
I'll comfort you

839
00:56:52,646 --> 00:56:54,248
Come here.

840
00:56:55,082 --> 00:56:56,116
It's cold.

841
00:56:57,584 --> 00:56:59,686
I'm going to the restroom for a bit.

842
00:57:12,533 --> 00:57:13,567
Turn around.

843
00:57:20,507 --> 00:57:22,042
Ten steps forward.

844
00:57:24,811 --> 00:57:27,080
- What's this?
- Hurry.

845
00:57:41,028 --> 00:57:43,597
Hey, it's Tak Mu I!

846
00:57:43,864 --> 00:57:45,332
The one who ran off with my book!

847
00:57:56,476 --> 00:57:58,178
How did you get here?

848
00:57:58,712 --> 00:58:00,881
Da Hong called and told me to pick her up.

849
00:58:02,983 --> 00:58:06,553
Since I'm already labeled a book thief,
I'll give it back in a few more days.

850
00:58:07,487 --> 00:58:11,258
I thought about getting it bound
or photocopied…

851
00:58:12,092 --> 00:58:13,827
but it felt disrespectful to the author.

852
00:58:15,062 --> 00:58:17,397
Right, that wouldn't be right.

853
00:58:18,799 --> 00:58:19,766
Instead,

854
00:58:21,902 --> 00:58:24,471
let's sing along to our heart's content.

855
00:58:27,808 --> 00:58:29,576
(Ian Kim Concert)

856
00:58:50,464 --> 00:58:53,333
What's wrong? Why are you crying?

857
00:58:54,268 --> 00:58:56,703
I cry when I'm drunk.

858
00:58:56,937 --> 00:58:58,505
You cry when you're drunk?

859
00:59:09,950 --> 00:59:14,288
(Epilogue)

860
00:59:14,288 --> 00:59:15,956
She's doing this again.

861
00:59:17,324 --> 00:59:19,793
Looks like I need to carry her.
Could you help?

862
00:59:21,495 --> 00:59:23,630
She wasn't this drunk before.

863
00:59:24,865 --> 00:59:26,500
Da Hong, snap out of it.

864
00:59:26,900 --> 00:59:28,001
Come on, hop on.

865
00:59:37,177 --> 00:59:39,746
Hey, I'll head in first. Take care.

866
00:59:46,195 --> 00:59:47,754
How much did you drink? Goodness.

867
00:59:53,086 --> 00:59:55,346
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
